.TH SDL_PROP_NAME_STRING 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_PROP_NAME_STRING \- A generic property for naming things.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_properties.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_PROP_NAME_STRING \(dqSDL.name\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This property is intended to be added to any
.BR SDL_PropertiesID
that needs a generic name associated with the property set\[char46] It is not guaranteed that any property set will include this key, but it is convenient to have a standard key that any piece of code could reasonably agree to use\[char46]
.PP
For example, the properties associated with an
.BR SDL_Texture
might have a name string of \(dqplayer sprites\(dq, or an
.BR SDL_AudioStream
might have \(dqbackground music\(dq, etc\[char46] This might also be useful for an
.BR SDL_IOStream
to list the path to its asset\[char46]
.PP
There is no format for the value set with this key; it is expected to be human-readable and informational in nature, possibly for logging or debugging purposes\[char46]
.PP
SDL does not currently set this property on any objects it creates, but this may change in later versions; it is currently expected that apps and external libraries will take advantage of it, when appropriate\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

